crates/audits/op-ml/16_16_Improvement_Suggestions.md:1:1. Suggestion | Migrate ad-hoc Serde-based configuration definitions to formal Protocol Buffers or versioned JSON schemas with OSCAL compliance mapping. | Rationale | Currently, vectorization configurations and hardware execution parameters are modeled using standard, ad-hoc Rust structs (`VectorizationConfig` and `ExecutionProvider`) that are manually parsed from the environment. To adhere to a schema-as-code discipline, these configurations should be generated from versioned Protocol Buffer schemas (e.g., integrated into `op-dbus-model`). This ensures cross-language capability, deterministic schema validation, and allows mapping execution settings directly to OSCAL Component Definition schemas for security compliance auditing (e.g., verifying under what authorization boundaries GPU providers like CUDA or TensorRT are leveraged). | Example (crates/op-ml/src/config.rs:172)
